title ML-DSA keygen rung, doubled oracle GREEN across all three parameter sets
prompt Continue the loop Lindy-first crux-first on the crypto arc; Rye prioritized; approve my own design rounds and make progress before checking in; send each finished increment; stop at custody gates.
think With the ML-DSA ring, encode, and sample all GREEN and sent, the next Lindy-first crux is rung 4 — the keygen, the ML-DSA sibling of mlkem_keygen.rye and the ladder's FIRST rung with a doubled oracle. Read the pivot doc (20260816-161537) which names it, then the vendored Zig ml_dsa newKeyFromSeed to fix the exact composition: crh(128, xi || k || l) via SHAKE256 splitting into rho(32) || rho'(64) || K(32), ExpandA with nonce (i<<8)|j so the seed bytes are (j, i), ExpandS with s1 nonces 0..l-1 and s2 nonces l..l+k-1, computeT = InvNTT(A dot NTT(s1)) + s2, Power2Round per coefficient, pk = rho || SimpleBitPack(t1, 10), tr = H(pk, 64), sk = rho || K || tr || BitPack(s1) || BitPack(s2) || BitPack(t0).
think Confirmed the parameter table from Zig: ML-DSA-44 k=4 l=4 eta=2, ML-DSA-65 k=6 l=5 eta=4, ML-DSA-87 k=8 l=7 eta=2; pk = 32 + 320k, sk = 128 + eta_packed*(l+k) + 416k, eta_packed 96 (eta 2) or 128 (eta 4). My mldsa_encode.rye is cleanly FIPS-faithful with signed conventions, so rather than mirror Zig's internal Q+eta-c representation I compose the spec's own SimpleBitPack/BitPack/power2round and lift each small secret from its residue form (0..eta or q-eta..q-1) to the centered [-eta, eta] value with to_signed_eta before packing. That keeps the standard-domain arithmetic auditable and takes parity only at the published byte boundary, exactly as the pivot doc foretold.
think Authored crypto/mldsa_keygen.rye composing only GREEN rungs (ring, encode, sample, shake) — no std.crypto in the keygen path; only the selftest invokes Zig as the parity oracle. One build fix: `packed` is a Zig keyword, renamed the pack locals to bytes_out. Buffers sized to the ceilings (max_k 8, max_l 7, pk_max 2592, sk_max 4896).
obs GREEN byte-for-byte against Zig std.crypto sign.mldsa newKeyFromSeed then toBytes at ALL THREE parameter sets over 8 deterministic seeds each — pk and sk both. The doubled oracle the ML-DSA ladder was waiting for: standard-domain composition and Montgomery-domain reference agree at the published boundary, the ring's coefficient ordering, the (j,i) matrix indexing, the RejBoundedPoly nonce sequence, Power2Round, and the whole pk/sk serialization all confirmed at once. A trivial all-zero key is refused before the diff.
obs TAME style bans clean; width-check exit 0; every function carries contract asserts with positive // invariant comments, every loop names its bound. README synced same round with the fourth ML-DSA rung row.
loom witness=crypto_mldsa_keygen_witness param_sets=3 seeds_each=8 pk_bytes_max=2592 sk_bytes_max=4896 wall_note=GREEN-after-keyword-rename
